id: pm-beads-1hs9
title: Send acknowledged Beads changes as compact field operations
description: "Generate field operations between two acknowledged Beads snapshots, with explicit removals, source/base digests and a full-snapshot fallback when the base is unavailable. Acceptance: two changed fields among 1,000 records emit exactly two operations plus identity receipts; replay is a no-op; an incorrect base refuses without altering either side. Include typed SDK and CLI, strict bounded validation, property tests, no-git public tracker measurements and npm/Bun CI evidence."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:00:36.905Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T22:11:22.498Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:01:02.491Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core SDK history and certified complete reads provide revisions and tracker data; Beads reconciliation consumes full snapshots; pending transfer preserves dependency closure; pm-vcs storage and pm-csv import own different boundaries. None supplies acknowledged outbound field operations. Design: a pure, bounded snapshot protocol reuses Beads acknowledgements and existing normalization, emits explicit unset/remove operations and source/base/target receipts, reconstructs a full snapshot before existing reconciliation. No new mutable outbox, lease, checkpoint or tracker mutation path."
  "2026-10-25T22:09:52.930Z",codex-agent,"Implemented stateless typed outbound generation/replay and CLI aliases. Reused the existing acknowledgement digest in persistence and validation. Exact-base inheritance avoids resending unchanged bindings. Targeted protocol suite: 5 tests pass; outgoing module has 100% measured lines, branches and functions. Public read-only no-git copy: 103 records, exactly 2 operations, 1701-byte delta versus 72261-byte full snapshot, unchanged bytes and source tree, replay/no-base fallback verified, wrong-base refused. Seeded SDK state differential and compiled CLI checks are in progress."
  "2026-10-25T22:11:20.966Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: with tests unchanged, reverting only the generateBeadsOutgoingDelta field-change condition to suppress updates makes the 1,000-record acceptance regression fail (expected two field operations, actual zero). Restore passes 5/5; targeted outgoing coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. Real compiled CLI passes JSON, TOON, replay and wrong-base checks without git. SDK-configured custom status test passes 32 randomized role registries; transport preserves opaque status values without lifecycle filtering. No mutable shared protocol state exists, so no new lease/journal/retry ownership path is added."
